<article class="env-example" id="06SS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06SS">Example <span data-tag="06SS">90.11.12</span>.</a> The computation of Example <a href="/tag/06IC" data-tag="06IC">90.11.11</a> simplifies in the classical case. Namely, in this case the tangent space of the functor $F = \underline{S}|_{\mathcal{C}_\Lambda }$ is simply the relative cotangent space of $S$ over $\Lambda $, in a formula $TF = T_{S/\Lambda }$. In fact, this works more generally when the field extension $k/k'$ is separable. See Exercises, Exercise <a href="/tag/029E" data-tag="029E">111.35.2</a>. </p>
</article>